@host = http://localhost:5000

# These tests expect exactly the 4 products from seed-products.http (SEED1-SEED5 done, nothing else in the products collection).
# Newest first, that order is: emperor bed, armchair, albany sectional, accent chair.
# No token is needed, anyone can browse.
#
# Every answer has these fields:
#   products     the products on THIS page
#   count        how many products are on this page
#   total        how many products exist
#   page         the page you asked for (1 if you did not say)
#   limit        products per page (10 if you did not say)
#   totalPages   how many pages there are with this limit


### PAGE1. No query -> 200, count 4, total 4, page 1, limit 10, totalPages 1
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products

### PAGE2. Two per page -> 200, emperor bed + armchair, count 2, total 4, limit 2, totalPages 2
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?limit=2

### PAGE3. Second page -> 200, albany sectional + accent chair, page 2
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?page=2&limit=2

### PAGE4. A page after the last one -> 200 (not an error), "products": [], count 0, total still 4
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?page=3&limit=2

### PAGE5. One per page -> 200, count 1, totalPages 4
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?limit=1

### PAGE6. Unknown query names are ignored -> 200, same as PAGE1
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?color=red

### PAGE7. The biggest page size allowed -> 200, limit 100
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?limit=100


### -------- wrong values: all 400 --------

### PAGE8. page=0 -> 400 "page must be a whole number from 1 to 100000"
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?page=0

### PAGE9. page=-1 -> 400, same message
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?page=-1

### PAGE10. page=abc -> 400, same message
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?page=abc

### PAGE11. page=1.5 -> 400, same message
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?page=1.5

### PAGE12. page is empty -> 400, same message
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?page=

### PAGE13. page sent twice -> 400, same message
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?page=1&page=2

### PAGE14. A page number that is too big -> 400, same message
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?page=100001

### PAGE15. limit=0 -> 400 "limit must be a whole number from 1 to 100"
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?limit=0

### PAGE16. limit=101 -> 400, same message
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?limit=101

### PAGE17. limit=ten -> 400, same message
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products?limit=ten
